      "thesis": "Monero is the stronger private-money system in practice: privacy is mandatory, fungibility is native, and the entire transaction graph is designed around default confidentiality. Zcash has stronger zero-knowledge primitives in isolation but optional transparency, shielded-pool boundary leakage, and substantially greater protocol complexity. The current valuation gap therefore looks wider than the fundamental privacy gap.",
